## MCP Server Tools Available

The following MCP tools are available to assist with this project:

### Project-Specific MCP Tools (word-pairing-mcp)
- **search_game_content** - Search across all CSV data files for matching words, categories, or definitions
- **validate_manifest** - Validate metadata.json and level structure for consistency
- **analyze_level_progression** - Analyze the deterministic level sequence to understand mode distribution and progression
- **audit_csv_consistency** - Check for duplicate entries, missing fields, or structural issues in CSV data files
- **find_unused_categories** - Find categories in the CSV data that aren't referenced by any level
- **audit_component_conventions** - Workflow 1: Scan all React components for .clinerules compliance — import ordering, touch targets (min-w-[48px] min-h-[48px]), aria-labels on icon-only buttons, neon color scheme usage, and naming conventions
- **validate_data_pipeline** - Workflow 2: Cross-validate localStorage schema, game-mode-to-data-source mappings (rule #11), CSV format spec adherence, and word tile uniqueness (rule #8)
- **audit_level_coverage** - Workflow 3: Cross-reference DETERMINISTIC_LEVEL_SEQUENCE against component files, verify data-source mappings exist, detect stub/incomplete components, and produce a prioritized PORTING_ROADMAP.md coverage gap report

### Build Pipeline MCP Tools (build-pipeline-mcp-server)
- **bump_version** - Bump the app version in capacitor.config.json, package.json, and build.gradle
- **validate_build** - Run `npm run build` and validate output
- **validate_capacitor_config** - Validate Capacitor configuration for Android
- **check_admob_ids** - Check AdMob ad unit IDs (test vs production)
- **generate_changelog** - Generate changelog from git history
- **verify_dist** - Verify dist/ build output directory
- **full_build_audit** - Complete build and release audit
- **diagnose_theme_data** - Diagnose themed level data loading issues
- **verify_mode_names** - Verify header mode name consistency across all components (checks MODE_NAME_COLORS in Header.tsx, displayModeName in Level1_Standard.tsx, modeNames in all level components, and .clinerules documentation)

### General MCP Tools
- **git** (`github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/tree/main/src/git`) — Git status, diff, commit, branch, log, show
- **sequentialthinking** (`github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/tree/main/src/sequentialthinking`) — Multi-step reasoning and problem-solving

